As for the `getHost()` method in this example, it is not implemented as we don't have a specific implementation of `host()` function. However, you can use the `netty` library to implement this.

```java
import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import netty.ftp.client.FTPClient;

@SpringBootApplication
public class WebServerApplication {

    @GetMapping("/path1")
    public String getFullUrlPath1() {
        return "http://example.com/path1";
    }

    @GetMapping("/path2")
    public String getFullUrlPath2() {
        return "http://example.com/path2";
    }

    private String host() {
        FTPClient ftp = new FTPClient();
        try {
            ftp.connect("ftp.example.com"); // replace with your FTP server
            System.out.println(ftp.getSession().getServerName());
            return ftp.getSession().getServerName();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(WebServerApplication.class, args);
    }
}
```
